    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d656">

                <pb facs="0700" n="686" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg686"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.20 Defense/10–444: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Chile</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-06T16:00:00-04:00">October 6, 1944—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1058. ReEmbs 1585 October 4, noon.<anchor n="45" xml:id="d656-f1"/> Difficulty
                    which has suddenly developed here necessitates postponement of staff talks. War
                    and Navy Departments have informed General Brett and Captain Stone.</p>
                <p>Please convey Department’s regrets to Fernández,<anchor n="46" xml:id="d656-f2"/>
                    explaining that delay is only temporary.</p>
                <p>Your instructions will be sent as soon as possible. In the meantime you may wish
                    to ask Military or Naval Attaché to show you copy of basic mimeographed
                        instructions<anchor n="47" xml:id="d656-f3"/> for officers holding staff
                    conversations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d656-f1" n="45" xml:id="d656-f1-content">
